# Testing Authoring Rules (StyleUp)

## Test placement
- Unit tests live alongside code under `src/` as `*.spec.ts` when practical.
- E2E tests live under `test/` as `*.e2e-spec.ts`.

## Unit test quality
- Test the **service-layer business logic** (not adapter wiring).
- Mock **port tokens** (e.g. `USER_REPOSITORY`, `OTP_STORE`, `TOKEN_SERVICE`), not ORM/Mongoose/Redis clients directly.
- Avoid low-value tests that only restate implementation (assert observable behavior and error codes).

## E2E test quality
- Use `supertest` with the Nest HTTP server and validate the mobile API envelope (`success`, `data`, `error.code`, `error.message`).
- Prefer the shared e2e helpers in `test/helpers` over ad-hoc setup/teardown.

## Never skip silently
- If verification cannot run (missing Docker, failed migrations, connectivity), your response must state:
  - which command failed
  - what it failed to connect to
  - the next action required (e.g. run `pnpm run test:e2e:prep` again)

